(a) Upon approval of the board of commissioners, the director of public works or a designee thereof, is authorized to designate and maintain by appropriate traffic-control signs, signals, markings and devices:
(1) Crosswalks at intersections where there is particular danger to pedestrians crossing the roadway;
(2) Other safety zones for pedestrians;
(3) Traffic lanes;
(4) Speed, parking or other traffic-control zones;
(5) Stop, yield, one-way and other directional devices; and
(6) Any other sign, signal, marking or device or creating any zone necessary for orderly and safe conditions on the roads and streets of the county.
(b) All traffic-control signs, signals, devices and markings shall conform to specifications in the "Manual on Uniform Traffic Control Devices" adopted by the state department of transportation. All signs and signals required hereunder for a particular purpose shall so far as practicable be uniform as to type and location throughout the county. All traffic-control devices so erected and not inconsistent with the provisions of state law or this Code shall be official traffic-control devices of the county.
(c) The county traffic engineer shall keep and maintain one (1) or more official maps or descriptions setting out all traffic zones, markings, signs and other traffic-control devices. The maps and any amendments or changes thereto shall be adopted by resolution of the board of commissioners. An official copy thereof shall be available to the public; and copies certified by the county clerk shall be admissible in court as proof of the location of any traffic zone, or marking, sign or other traffic-control device.
(d) No person shall be charged with violating a traffic zone, or marking, sign, signal or other traffic control device unless appropriate signs, signals, markings or devices are in fact operating or in existence on the streets involved.
(e) Any violation of any traffic zone, marking, sign, signal or other traffic-control device established hereunder shall be a violation of this Code.
(Code 1979, § 8-1-3)
